re. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Postal Realty Trust, Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $962M market cap on $96M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +22% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +5.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $38M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 39 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.15\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 1.7% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 3.9% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 13% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Growing faster than most Real Estate peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(PSTL) Movement as an Input in Quant Signal Sets","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/12/PSTL_Movement_as_an_Input_in_Quant_Signal_Sets_111326035602_1794560162.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794560162.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Postal Realty Trust Inc (PSTL) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Record Acquisitions, Raised ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/real-estate/articles/postal-realty-trust-inc-pstl-210924595.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793826564.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.844,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Postal Realty Trust targets $185M-$200M 2026 acquisitions as it raises AFFO guidance to $1.42-$1.44 per share (NYSE:PSTL)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4665495-postal-realty-trust-targets-185m-200m-2026-acquisitions-as-it-raises-affo-guidance-to-1_42","date":"2026-11-04"